{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces","id":1339108,"title":"Can \"turn momentum \" affect living beings as well?(forces)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-02T20:15:23-07:00","id":1339108,"title":"Can \"turn momentum \" affect living beings as well?(forces)","content":"Hi guys <br /> <br /> As the title says, me and my friends were wondering if the spell &quot;turn momentum&quot; would be able to stop an assailant and affect living beings as well. When i say living beings, i mean melee attackers who swing at you or try to punch you or grapple you and have a body and a will to kill you. The issue came up when the obrimos of the group tried to use the spell to redirect and enemy attack, it was a punch from a vampire with vigor. Then the second time he tried to use it to avoid getting hit by a gangrel. (It was an over the top bloody story of revenge a la &quot; kill bill style&quot; where some vampires killed his entire cabal). <br /> <br /> My opinion is that it probably would affect living beings as well, since everything in this world that has a mass and speed and is moving in space and time has a &quot;momentum to turn&quot; and that includes living beings as well. Since forces controls every physical manifestation of forces, the effects of turn momentum should apply also to objects that are moving, whether they are alive or not. Any thoughts ? <br /> <br /> If for any reason turn momentum turned out to be off limits for redirecting or affecting human beings, then i would argue that by the same principle affecting the gravity of an area shouldnt affect the living beings that are standing in that area during the spell, since they are not under the pure purview of the forces arcanum (a paradox of course and a nonsens everybody knows that people just fall off into the sky when gravity is reversed).<br /> <br /> Please bear with us cause the text of the actual spell is ambiguous to us and english is not our first language. It does not clearly talk about living beings ir physical attacks from living beings, just &quot;moving objects&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's the text:<br /> <br /> Turn Momentum (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Athletics, Firearms, Science<br /> This spell allows the mage to redirect a target\u2019s momentum. <br /> Usually this forms a shield against projectiles, but it can be used <br /> on larger objects, as well. When a mage could use her Defense <br /> against an object, she may use this spell instead to redirect it as <br /> an instant action. If cast with a prolonged Duration, the mage <br /> may take a Dodge action each turn and use this spell instead of <br /> receiving the normal benefits for Dodging.<br /> The spell allows the mage to turn a number of moving objects <br /> up to Potency. She does not have fine control over where each <br /> object is deflected, and the spell cannot make objects reverse <br /> direction entirely, only veer off target. The maximum Size of <br /> a redirected object is determined by the spell\u2019s Scale factor. <br /> Because the spell acts upon an object\u2019s momentum and not the <br /> object itself, the weight and speed are irrelevant to this spell\u2019s <br /> effect; if the mage can use the spell, the magic will thwart any <br /> object within its parameters. The redirected object maintains all <br /> its original momentum. By default, the Storyteller determines <br /> a random direction for the object to travel when redirected.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage can use Turn Momentum\u2019s effect as a <br /> reflexive action instead. <br /> +1 Reach: The mage may control where the object is redi-<br /> rected to, as long as it is within 90 degrees of the original arc <br /> in any direction.<br /> +2 Reach: The object\u2019s momentum can be fully reversed. <br /> Thrown and Ranged weapons strike their users.<br /> Add Time \u2022: With Time 1 and a Reach, the mage can turn <br /> objects too fast for her to gain Defense against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","user":"Lasombra","date":". 10-03-2019, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T21:55:09-07:00","id":1339124,"title":"","content":"Vampires aren't living beings.<br /> <br /> That aside, Turn Momentum works on anything with a momentum so long as it is within the size scale factor of the spell, this includes both the living and the undead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T22:24:45-07:00","id":1339125,"title":"","content":"I don't think it would work on melee attackers as they should count as one object. A fist would start veering off as the momentum of the attacker shifts, but their position wouldn't shift that much and the arm could still extend in the same direction. Unfortunately Turn Momentum doesn't have any way to model the added difficulty of hitting you when your body starts shifting to the side without having a second effect alongside what's already written so I'm inclined to just say that it doesn't work on grounded melee attacks.<br /> A charging attacker or someone who literally jumps at you is a different thing. They'd fly to the side, probably being knocked prone in the attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T23:11:03-07:00","id":1339131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339125#post1339125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it would work on melee attackers as they should count as one object. A fist would start veering off as the momentum of the attacker shifts, but their position wouldn't shift that much and the arm could still extend in the same direction. Unfortunately Turn Momentum doesn't have any way to model the added difficulty of hitting you when your body starts shifting to the side without having a second effect alongside what's already written so I'm inclined to just say that it doesn't work on grounded melee attacks.<br /> A charging attacker or someone who literally jumps at you is a different thing. They'd fly to the side, probably being knocked prone in the attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i think it would only work on &quot;throwed&quot; living being, because the subject would rapidly correct a melee blow going in the wrong direction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T01:15:03-07:00","id":1339142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339124#post1339124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires aren't living beings.<br /> <br /> That aside, Turn Momentum works on anything with a momentum so long as it is within the size scale factor of the spell, this includes both the living and the undead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a good argument lol maybe i should specify if it can affect &quot;moving enemies trying to hit u?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T09:28:27-07:00","id":1339201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339142#post1339142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats a good argument lol maybe i should specify if it can affect &quot;moving enemies trying to hit u?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It should work on anything coming at you. To <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24346_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24346\" data-vbnamecard=\"24346\">Neos01</a>'s statement I say this: deflecting blows is a key part of martial arts and a sudden alteration of the trajectory of the swing would probably throw the attacker off balance, forget being able to correct mid swing the best case scenario for the attacker is merely having to start the attack over (which would require another round).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T10:55:03-07:00","id":1339215,"title":"","content":"I would say it works as you describe, OP. Though, making someone punch/kick themselves in the face is unlikely to happen(because of body mechanics), you could probably just say it hurts them from the pure reversal of force/forcing the target's limbs to move backwards(probably in unnatural directions). Flying kick/tackles would result in knocked down tilt as well returning to where they jumped from if reversed completely. Honestly most full reversal probably would cause this against a melee attacker. Game mechanics and fairness may be the only reason you don't do this(though if it makes the scene, cooler/more cinematic...why not?)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2757\" data-vbnamecard=\"2757\">proindrakenzol</a> has the right idea here. We already know because of martial arts what happens when you redirect the force behind a blow. Many techniques are centered around exactly this and if used correctly are extremely difficult to react to if you don't know how(or you don't see it coming). Usually, &quot;countering&quot; such a deflection requires simply going with the new flow of energy and using it somehow, such as turning the redirected flow of a forward punch into a spinning backhand with the other fist or something.<br /> <br /> Cool idea: Have the player wreck most people with their own blows except master of martial arts that would make sense to you, prompting a kind of real-time martial arts Mystery.<br /> <br /> Oh and keep in mind that while this spell is awesome defensively, it's effects are pretty obviously supernatural. Against a bunch of Vampires this wont be a problem, but if they bring a cadre of blood-bonded normies, a wisdom check/quiescence may come into play. And fighting in an area with cameras could make this an ongoing issue every time someone reviews that security tape/looks at the feed. Also: keep in mind that this spell cant actually be cast reflexively. You can just turn that dodge action into a reflexive action to get the effects instead when you cast with prolonged duration. So unless your player is acting first, he might still get hurt badly the first turn. And this spell is also potentially gonna cost quite a bit of reach which will mean probably Paradox or a lot of Mana cost.<br /> <br /> Basically, keep in mind the spells actual limitations. You may be right that this spell will work as you say, but it is far from a perfect solution to a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24407-radriel7","name":"Radriel7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24407_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T12:45:34-07:00","id":1339229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339201#post1339201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It should work on anything coming at you. To <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>'s statement I say this: deflecting blows is a key part of martial arts and a sudden alteration of the trajectory of the swing would probably throw the attacker off balance, forget being able to correct mid swing the best case scenario for the attacker is merely having to start the attack over (which would require another round).</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but to defend against a melee blow you redirect only the body part that is attacking.<br /> The reason i think that the spell would not work is that it must redirect the momentum of the whole body, and only for the moment before the impact.<br /> So, excluding a charge or a jump attack the effect on the attacker would be difficult to apply, as a melee attack are a combination of different momentum in different moments.<br /> That said i m not saiyng that force cannot block melee attacks, but probably a more complex spell is required","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T13:29:59-07:00","id":1339232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339229#post1339229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but to defend against a melee blow you redirect only the body part that is attacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Not always.<br /> 2) When you do it's due to practical limitation, not because you wouldn't want to redirect their whole body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason i think that the spell would not work is that it must redirect the momentum of the whole body, and only for the moment before the impact. </div> </div> </div>There is nothing in the description that would preclude changing the momentum of only a single portion of a non-rigid body, the only requirement is that the whole body must fall within the size limits of the spell.<br /> <br /> If the spell only affected an object an infinitesimal period before impact it would be worthless, it obviously works enough before the impact that it could deflect, say, a speeding motorcycle; with Reach (or Time/Fate Mage Armor) it can also affect bullets which would need to be deflected even further away from the body.<br /> <br /> Finally, angular momentum is still momentum, and altering the angular momentum of a human (or vampire) swinging a fist would certainly be capable of causing a miss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, excluding a charge or a jump attack the effect on the attacker would be difficult to apply, as a melee attack are a combination of different momentum in different moments.<br /> That said i m not saiyng that force cannot block melee attacks, but probably a more complex spell is required </div> </div> </div>And I'm saying that's nonsense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T20:37:30-07:00","id":1339301,"title":"","content":"If you are using a spell on a vampire (as in OP) I would think that there would at least be a Contest of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T22:08:34-07:00","id":1339310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339301#post1339301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are using a spell on a vampire (as in OP) I would think that there would at least be a Contest of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clash of Wills only occurs if there are two powers that cannot coexist, so unless the Vampire had a Discipline or Devotion that prevented their momentum from being altered there would be no basis for a Clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T00:31:50-07:00","id":1339314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339232#post1339232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Not always.<br /> 2) When you do it's due to practical limitation, not because you wouldn't want to redirect their whole body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is nothing in the description that would preclude changing the momentum of only a single portion of a non-rigid body, the only requirement is that the whole body must fall within the size limits of the spell.<br /> <br /> If the spell only affected an object an infinitesimal period before impact it would be worthless, it obviously works enough before the impact that it could deflect, say, a speeding motorcycle; with Reach (or Time/Fate Mage Armor) it can also affect bullets which would need to be deflected even further away from the body.<br /> <br /> Finally, angular momentum is still momentum, and altering the angular momentum of a human (or vampire) swinging a fist would certainly be capable of causing a miss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I'm saying that's nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i ve rereaded this passage &quot;When a mage could use her Defense against an object, she may use this spell instead to redirect it as an instant action. &quot;<br /> So it seems it can be used on melee attacks, as the difference between an object and a living being has no effect on the momentum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T03:59:29-07:00","id":1339328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339232#post1339232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing in the description that would preclude changing the momentum of only a single portion of a non-rigid body, the only requirement is that the whole body must fall within the size limits of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing in the description that <i>allows</i> the spell to only affect a single portion of an object.<br /> <br /> <br /> The thing about projectiles is that they don't have contact with a medium that partially corrects their direction.<br /> If you can deflect only a portion of a body, say a fist, then you still have the forces imparted by the muscles that seek to correct the direction. The way you deflect a fist in martial arts is that you force it to a different direction. Using the spell like this should very much have a large impact on the attacker, but not automatically dodge the blow.<br /> And if you can't deflect a portion of a body (which is how I believe the spell works) you instead change the momentum of the whole person, which would cause an imbalance as they're yanked one way, but they still have the same facing and as long as they keep their footing they should at most get a small penalty (on top of the regular Defense) rather than getting to automatically dodge the blow.<br /> <br /> Since the effects on a projectile and on a blow from a grounded opponent should be very different and represented through different mechanical effects, the simplest way to handle it is to let the spell only work on projectiles and let melee attacks require a different spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T08:17:36-07:00","id":1339380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339301#post1339301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are using a spell on a vampire (as in OP) I would think that there would at least be a Contest of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>What power does the vampire have that specifically prevents its momentum from being redirected?<br /> <br /> Clash of Wills isn't just 'an extra barrier when you try to affect a supernatural subject'. It's for resolving conflicts when two discrete abilities come into conflict and there's no explicit path to resolution within their mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T10:04:52-07:00","id":1339397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339328#post1339328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's nothing in the description that <i>allows</i> the spell to only affect a single portion of an object.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there's no reason to think that such a restriction exists.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing about projectiles is that they don't have contact with a medium that partially corrects their direction. </div> </div> </div>Fun fact: you can twist an entire body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you can deflect only a portion of a body, say a fist, then you still have the forces imparted by the muscles that seek to correct the direction. </div> </div> </div>No, that's not how that works. If you're deflecting, rather than blocking, then the force behind the blow is tangential to the force that redirects the blow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way you deflect a fist in martial arts is that you force it to a different direction. </div> </div> </div>Using a force tangential to the motion of the fist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using the spell like this should very much have a large impact on the attacker, but not automatically dodge the blow. </div> </div> </div>The &quot;large impact&quot; should be dodging the blow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you can't deflect a portion of a body (which is how I believe the spell works) you instead change the momentum of the whole person, which would cause an imbalance as they're yanked one way, but they still have the same facing and as long as they keep their footing they should at most get a small penalty (on top of the regular Defense) rather than getting to automatically dodge the blow. </div> </div> </div>If you changed the momentum of the whole body they would absolutely miss because you would be changing their momentum such that they physically could not connect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since the effects on a projectile and on a blow from a grounded opponent should be very different and represented through different mechanical effects, the simplest way to handle it is to let the spell only work on projectiles and let melee attacks require a different spell. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Usually this forms a shield against projectiles, but it can be used<br /> on larger objects, as well.&quot;<br /> <br /> So it is not exclusively used on projectiles, and a person with a fist is certainly a &quot;larger object.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T14:57:49-07:00","id":1339448,"title":"","content":"thanks everyone for the inputs guys, u gave us much food for thoughts. I was thinking about allowing the spell to influence an attacker who is trying to hit a mage with melee or brawl attacks but allow the victim to whitstand the effects, maybe with stamina? I mean, if the spell really allows to automatically dodge every attack against the mage without any problem it looks pretty broken to us. Also, i was thinking about allow it to be whistood with stamina considering that the spell &quot;levitation&quot; (forces 4) actually allow a mage to influence and affect an entire target with forces and it's whitstood by the target stamina. After all, fine manipulation and control against a weaker and lighter opponent is something different from trying to dodge and turn the momentum of a much bigger and faster opponent, what do u guys think? <br /> <br /> Also, i think clash of wills would apply only with enemies using celerity or powers that allow them to interrumpt an action or attack suddenly out of nowhere, representing how &quot;quick&quot; the mage can react and use turn momentum to save his ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T19:15:51-07:00","id":1339499,"title":"","content":"Thinking things are &quot;broken&quot; in Mage is largely missing the point. Mages are supposed to be powerful. Typically, the only thing that's broken is when a mechanic isn't clear (The subject of this thread can be an example) or when they do not achieve the things the game of Mage wants them too. Being able to turn aside a fist is significantly less powerful than being able to turn aside a bullet when considering how much damage bullets usually do vs. how much a fist does so if you use this spell for that purpose I don't even see why you'd think it's &quot;broken&quot; by being too powerful.<br /> <br /> With this spell there's not really any reason to use Withstand, because the subject it's cast on is not the attacker, but the person being attacked. Levitation is the reverse case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T04:15:27-07:00","id":1339564,"title":"","content":"the problem is that ambiguous: &quot;bigger objects&quot;. If only it would explicilty say &quot;bigger objects including attacking adversaries, or people moving&quot; then the issue wouldn't pop up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T18:24:36-07:00","id":1339736,"title":"","content":"It doesn\u2019t say anything about bigger objects, it says that the size of the object that can be deflected is determined by Scale, and considering default Scale is Size 5 or smaller this spell can be used to deflect most melee attackers without worrying about whatever \u201cbigger\u201d means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T19:15:15-07:00","id":1339742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339131#post1339131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, i think it would only work on &quot;throwed&quot; living being, because the subject would rapidly correct a melee blow going in the wrong direction</div> </div> </div> </div>If my fist suddenly moved in a different direction, and assuming I have enough awareness to notice, I would be too startled to correct it. You would need specialized training (at least a one dot merit, probably more) to be able to react fast enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T02:22:13-07:00","id":1339789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1339742#post1339742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my fist suddenly moved in a different direction, and assuming I have enough awareness to notice, I would be too startled to correct it. You would need specialized training (at least a one dot merit, probably more) to be able to react fast enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, probably any kind of disturbance to a blow would deflect it.<br /> Apart from realism i think that the major doubt here is if the spell Turn momentum can handle melee blow or you would need another spell (any level 2 of force or other arcana could do it).<br /> As the rules written are not 100% clear probably the right approach would be for each GM to houserule it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T09:27:28-07:00","id":1339863,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m sorry, no, it is not unclear. The spell can clearly turn away bullets, and with increased Scale even speeding cars. Fists fall somewhere between those two sizes and so clearly can be deflected. The only confusion came because some of you decided to get way too into the weeds. Forest, trees, pick your metaphor I suppose, they make a lot of them for this kind of situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T07:07:51-07:00","id":1340022,"title":"","content":"Do u guys think a mage could react fast enough even when he is attacked by surprise or against an enemy that uses an effect like time acceleration to interrumpt his attack ? Would turn momentum still be able to deflect the attack? Cause i dont think it would.be possible, since it should only work when the mage could take a dodge action","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T08:18:13-07:00","id":1340033,"title":"","content":"Turn Momentum specifies you must be able to use your Defense and that then you have the option of using Turn Momentum instead. Some other Magic or merits let you use your Defense against things you normally couldn't, and maybe it could be argue about if that should apply to Turn Momentum as well, but that would depende of the specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T08:48:49-07:00","id":1340037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339108-can-turn-momentum-affect-living-beings-as-well-forces?p=1340022#post1340022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do u guys think a mage could react fast enough even when he is attacked by surprise or against an enemy that uses an effect like time acceleration to interrumpt his attack ? Would turn momentum still be able to deflect the attack? Cause i dont think it would.be possible, since it should only work when the mage could take a dodge action</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a section in the spell that already addresses this, you need Time 1 and a Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}